Package: backup-project-server
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Backup Project <noreply@example.invalid>
Homepage: https://github.com/PlyusWang/backup-project
Description: Backup Project server (BPSEC1 transport, BPSEC2 signed identity)
 Streaming backup storage server: BPNET1 protocol over BPSEC1
 (X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-CTR + HMAC-SHA256), with optional
 server identity certificates (BPCERT1) signed by an offline root.
 .
 The package installs the server, the on-host administration tools and
 the interactive admin menu, creates a system user "backup-project",
 and starts the service on 127.0.0.1:18765 only. Publishing the port to
 the internet is an explicit administrator action: it needs a
 certificate, a reason, and require_bpsec2 = true.
 .
 User data under /var/lib/backup-project-server is never removed by
 package operations. Use backup-server-purge-data for that.
